---
/* L23 - the transformer block: normalise, attend, keep, think, keep. */
---

<figure class="fig">
  <div class="fig__frame">
    <img
      class="fig__picture"
      src={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}illustrations/L23.jpg`}
      alt="A line drawing of an assembly line of identical small workbenches on a conveyor, each holding a sheet of paper, with a thick curved pipe looping under the belt and back up into the next bench, and a small side room with a blackboard attached to every other bench."
    />
    <svg
      class="fig__svg"
      viewBox="0 0 640 340"
      role="img"
      aria-labelledby="L23-fig-title L23-fig-desc"
    >
      <title id="L23-fig-title">One transformer block: normalise, attend, keep, think, keep</title>
      <desc id="L23-fig-desc">
        A horizontal flow diagram. The input vector x enters a layer norm box,
        then an attention box, then reaches a plus sign where a curved residual
        path brings the original x back around from below. The result enters a
        second layer norm box, then an MLP box, then reaches a second plus sign
        with a second curved residual path returning to it, and the block output
        leaves to the right. Both plus signs are drawn as circles with a cross
        inside.
      </desc>

      <!-- the flow line -->
      <g class="fig-flow">
        <path d="M24 128 H616" />
      </g>

      <!-- the boxes -->
      <g class="fig-box">
        <rect x="34" y="98" width="76" height="60" />
        <rect x="152" y="98" width="76" height="60" />
        <rect x="368" y="98" width="76" height="60" />
        <rect x="486" y="98" width="76" height="60" />
      </g>
      <text x="52" y="124" class="fig-text fig-text--ink">layer</text>
      <text x="48" y="140" class="fig-text fig-text--ink">norm</text>
      <text x="164" y="124" class="fig-text fig-text--ink">attend</text>
      <text x="160" y="140" class="fig-text fig-text--dim">q . k / sqrt(d_k)</text>
      <text x="380" y="124" class="fig-text fig-text--ink">layer</text>
      <text x="376" y="140" class="fig-text fig-text--ink">norm</text>
      <text x="496" y="124" class="fig-text fig-text--ink">mlp</text>
      <text x="494" y="140" class="fig-text fig-text--dim">4 x d_model</text>

      <!-- the adds -->
      <g class="fig-add">
        <circle cx="278" cy="128" r="18" />
        <circle cx="424" cy="128" r="18" />
      </g>
      <path d="M270 120 L286 136 M286 120 L270 136" class="fig-add-cross" />
      <path d="M416 120 L432 136 M432 120 L416 136" class="fig-add-cross" />

      <!-- the residual highways -->
      <g class="m-draw fig-residual" style="--m-length: 460; --m-duration: 1.6s; animation-delay: 0.5s">
        <path d="M24 128 V232 H278 V150" />
        <path d="M278 128 V232 H424 V150" />
      </g>
      <text x="60" y="252" class="fig-text fig-text--dim">residual: the input rides around the side</text>

      <!-- the input and the output -->
      <text x="24" y="82" class="fig-label">x</text>
      <text x="596" y="82" class="fig-label">out</text>
      <g class="fig-flow">
        <path d="M596 92 V98" />
        <path d="M596 98 l-3 -6 h6 z" class="fig-flow-head" />
      </g>

      <!-- the shape rule -->
      <g>
        <rect x="24" y="272" width="592" height="44" class="fig-panel" />
        <text x="38" y="290" class="fig-text fig-text--ink">every box keeps the shape n x d_model</text>
        <text x="38" y="308" class="fig-text fig-text--num">n tokens in, n tokens out, width unchanged</text>
      </g>
    </svg>
  </div>
  <figcaption class="fig__caption">
    <span class="edge-code">figure L23</span>
    <span class="fig__caption-text">A transformer block normalises the vector, attends, adds the original back, then does the same around the MLP, and every stage returns a vector of the same shape.</span>
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .fig-label {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.09em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    fill: var(--color-ink-45);
  }

  .fig-text {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    fill: var(--color-ink-70);
  }

  .fig-text--ink {
    fill: var(--color-ink);
  }

  .fig-text--dim {
    fill: var(--color-ink-45);
  }

  .fig-text--num {
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }

  .fig-flow path {
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--color-ink-45);
    stroke-width: 1;
  }

  .fig-flow .fig-flow-head {
    fill: var(--color-ink-45);
    stroke: none;
  }

  .fig-box rect {
    fill: var(--color-ground);
    stroke: var(--color-ink);
    stroke-width: 1;
  }

  .fig-add circle {
    fill: var(--color-ground);
    stroke: var(--color-ink);
    stroke-width: 1;
  }

  .fig-add-cross {
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--color-ink);
    stroke-width: 1;
  }

  .fig-residual path {
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--color-prussian);
    stroke-width: 1;
  }

  .fig-panel {
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--color-rule-soft);
    stroke-width: 1;
  }
</style>
